# Contact chat: sends each message to your inbox through Resend.
# Copy this file to .env.local for local runs, and set the same variables
# in your host's dashboard (Vercel: Project > Settings > Environment
# Variables) for the live site. Never commit a real key, and never put a
# secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable: those are compiled into the
# JavaScript every visitor downloads.

# Required. Create one at https://resend.com/api-keys with "Sending access"
# only. Without it the chat still works, but every send answers
# "not_configured" and the visitor is offered their own email app instead.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional. Where messages are delivered. Defaults to identity.email in
# lib/content.ts.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Optional. Who the messages come from. Defaults to
# "Portfolio <onboarding@resend.dev>", Resend's shared test sender, which
# can only deliver to the email address your Resend account was created
# with. To send from your own address or to any other inbox, verify a
# domain in Resend and use an address on it, for example:
#   Portfolio <contact@yourdomain.com>
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Portfolio <onboarding@resend.dev>

# Development only, for testing without a real key: sends to a local mock
# server instead of Resend. Ignored when NODE_ENV is "production" and for
# any host other than 127.0.0.1, localhost or [::1]. Leave it unset.
# CONTACT_UPSTREAM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010/emails
